# LangChain platform (official docs)

- **Canonical entry**: [Docs by LangChain](https://docs.langchain.com/) — observability (LangSmith), evaluation, prompts, deployment, and open-source agent stacks.
- **Full page index for agents / search**: [`https://docs.langchain.com/llms.txt`](https://docs.langchain.com/llms.txt) — use this before guessing URLs or behavior.
- **JavaScript / TypeScript OSS docs root**: paths under [`/oss/javascript/`](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/concepts/products.md) (LangChain, LangGraph, Deep Agents, integrations).

## Choose the right layer (TypeScript)

Per [Frameworks, runtimes, and harnesses](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/concepts/products.md):

| Layer | Product | Prefer when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Framework** | [LangChain (JS)](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langchain/overview) | Quick agents, shared abstractions (models, tools, agent loop, middleware); LangChain sits on LangGraph—you do not have to expose graph details for simple agents. |
| **Runtime** | [LangGraph (JS)](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/overview) | Fine-grained orchestration, **durable execution**, streaming, persistence, human-in-the-loop at the graph level, production-oriented graphs. |
| **Harness** | [Deep Agents (JS)](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/deepagents/overview) | Long-running, complex multi-step work: planning, subagents, filesystem-style context, predefined tooling—built on LangGraph. |

- **Providers / models**: [Providers and models](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/concepts/providers-and-models.md) — one integration surface across vendors.
- **Integrations**: [LangChain JS integrations hub](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/integrations/providers/overview.md); add or debug tools against specific provider pages listed there—not from memory alone.

## LangSmith (commercial platform)

- Use LangSmith docs under [`/langsmith/`](https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/deployment.md) for **tracing**, **datasets**, **evaluators**, **deployment** (including Agent Server, threads/runs/streaming MCP, hybrid/self-hosted).
- Typical concerns: instrumentation / custom spans ([annotate code](https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/annotate-code.md)), metadata/tags, feedback, RBAC/auth, Agent Server scaling and checkpointer/store configuration.

## Agent implementation habits

- Prefer linking behavior to the **current** doc page rather than citing deprecated blog posts; APIs move—verify against `/oss/javascript/` or `/langsmith/` as needed.
- For NestJS backends wrapping agents: keep thin HTTP layers and put orchestration in injectable services; wire LangSmith tracing via env (`LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`, `LANGCHAIN_TRACING_*` / LangSmith vars per [environment variables](https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/env-var.md)) without hardcoding secrets.
- When behavior is unclear, fetch or search **`llms.txt`** and open the closest matching markdown path rather than improvising signatures.
